{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfkqv8v7UGZ5NJBtbxU7d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the convergence problem with the `fifo_memory_buffer_judgment` repair candidate, and the admission check now prints `OK`. All three files are written in `candidate_0_repair_1/`.\n\n**What was wrong:** The buffer-capacity span `kappa` had an unbounded Normal prior. Above about 8.5 every capacity setting holds the whole sequence, so the likelihood goes flat there. The chains ended up in different regions, which gave the R-hat of 1.53 and bulk ESS of 7.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- `kappa` is now `2 + 7·sigmoid(z_kappa)` with `z_kappa ~ Normal(0, 1)`, which keeps it between 2 and 9.\n- The trial-to-trial spread in buffer capacity is wider and smoother (SD 1.5 instead of 1).\n- The rest of the model is unchanged: the second-order chance coin against the regular generators, evidence weighed per held flip, and per-person signed sensitivity, switch belief and side habit.\n\n**Diagnostic fit** (4 chains, 400 tune + 400 draws, on the real responses):\n- 0 divergent transitions.\n- Max R-hat is 1.03 overall; it is 1.00 for most top-level parameters, `sigma_side` is 1.02 and some per-person parameters reach 1.03.\n- Minimum bulk ESS is 291 (`sigma_side`), and 712 across the per-person parameters.\n- The fit took about 11 minutes on one CPU, well inside the 30-minute admission limit.\n\nThese were shorter chains than the admission fit, so passing the stricter 1.05 R-hat threshold there is likely but not certain.\n\n**The data mostly reject the forgetting idea.** `kappa` settles at about 8.8, against its upper bound. That means people mostly hold the whole sequence, and only about a fifth of trials on length-8 pairs are judged on a cut-down buffer. I reworded `hypothesis.md` so it no longer claims a span of \"roughly four to seven flips\". The model may therefore predict close to the incumbent. I haven't checked novelty, so it could still be rejected as a near-duplicate. Two other differences from the incumbent should help it stay distinct: its motif suspicion is shared rather than per-person, and it keeps the heads-leaning trick coin.\n\n**Other results from the check:**\n- The smoke fit's ELPD-LOO was −3593.2, against −3568.2 for the best model.\n- PSIS-LOO was flagged unreliable on that 100-draw, 1-chain run (6% of trials with high Pareto k). That is common with this many per-person parameters on a short run and may not hold on the full fit.\n\nMy diagnostic script is still in `candidate_0_repair_1/scratch/`, because the command to delete it was denied. It doesn't affect admission."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":183,"cache_read_input_tokens":94384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":183,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":769,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c854474-bf2e-416f-868b-40395363d41f","uuid":"49c0bc7e-593d-4963-9848-37a4380a0298","timestamp":"2026-10-06T10:42:37.418Z","request_id":"req_011Cfkqv8Yn73motT3PKr88D"}
